analysis:
This batch contains documentation only. It adds changelog.d/qwen-missing-user-query-400.md (lines 1-7) and changes docs/architecture/inference.md (head hunks @@ -714 and @@ -1116). Both describe a new pre-render validation, Qwen35TemplateFixes.swift validateUserQuery. For qwen3_5, qwen3_5_moe and prism_hadamard_qwen35 histories with no user turn beyond <tool_response> wrappers, it returns a typed HTTP 400 missingUserQuery instead of the previous provider 500 template_render error.

Security relevance: the change is a client-error classification and fails closed before rendering. It plausibly reduces the provider-fault signals a malicious consumer (ADV-002) can cause. No changes to encryption (T-008), the prefix cache (T-041), attestation or authorization (TB-011) are visible.

The Swift implementation is not in this batch. The next pass should check that validateUserQuery:
- runs before any template render or model acquisition on both encrypted-coordinator and local StandaloneServer ingress;
- uses the same <tool_response> wrapper detection as the template, since a mismatch could still reach a template raise or reject valid requests;
- emits an error message that does not echo prompt content (A-001) into errors or logs;
- maps the 400 through the encrypted error path without a plaintext fallback (T-008);
- does not let 400s be counted as provider faults or reputation events, or affect billing.

No findings are raised from docs alone.
